{{!
    @template tool_lp/user_competency_course_navigation

    Jump to another participant or another competency of a course, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/user_competency_course_navigation of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500),
    admin/tool/lp/templates/user_competency_course_navigation.mustache. Re-diff it against that file on
    every core upgrade.

    Kept from core: the two selects' ids user-nav-<uniqid> and competency-nav-<uniqid>, which the
    JavaScript hands to tool_lp/user_competency_course_navigation and core/form-autocomplete, their
    labels and their form-select class, every option with its value and selected state, the form's
    class user-competency-course-navigation (core's tool_lp stylesheet hides the native selects by it;
    the autocomplete draws the visible control), the hidden fields userid, competencyid and courseid
    (no module reads them; kept as core has them), the group selector (core's own HTML,
    triple-stashed) and the JavaScript itself. The names keep core's escaping.
    Changed: the panel is the theme's (dim-comp-nav); the group selector sits in a div rather than a
    paragraph, because core's single_select markup is a form, which a paragraph cannot hold, and is
    left out when empty; the line break between the two selects is the panel's gap.
    The JavaScript is core's statement for statement, with the constructor's parameter capitalised
    (Nav) and one long line wrapped: core's copy has no example context, so the template lint never
    ran eslint over it.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * groupselector - HTML
    * userid, competencyid, courseid, baseurl - read by the JavaScript and the hidden fields
    * hasusers - boolean
    * users - array of id, selected, fullname
    * hascompetencies - boolean
    * competencies - array of id, selected, shortname, idnumber

    Example context (json):
    {
        "groupselector": "",
        "userid": 3,
        "competencyid": 1,
        "courseid": 2,
        "baseurl": "https://example.com/admin/tool/lp/user_competency_in_course.php",
        "hasusers": true,
        "users": [
            {"id": 3, "fullname": "Sam Student", "selected": true},
            {"id": 4, "fullname": "Robin Learner", "selected": false}
        ],
        "hascompetencies": true,
        "competencies": [
            {"id": 1, "shortname": "Communicate clearly", "idnumber": "COMM-1", "selected": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav float-sm-end">
{{#groupselector}}
<div class="dim-comp-nav__group">{{{groupselector}}}</div>
{{/groupselector}}
<form class="user-competency-course-navigation">
<input type="hidden" name="userid" value="{{userid}}">
<input type="hidden" name="competencyid" value="{{competencyid}}">
<input type="hidden" name="courseid" value="{{courseid}}">
{{#hasusers}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="user-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}jumptouser, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select id="user-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="form-select">
{{#users}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{fullname}}</option>
{{/users}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hasusers}}
{{#hascompetencies}}
<span class="dim-comp-nav__group">
<label for="competency-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="accesshide">{{#str}}jumptocompetency, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
<select id="competency-nav-{{uniqid}}" class="form-select">
{{#competencies}}
<option value="{{id}}" {{#selected}}selected="selected"{{/selected}}>{{{shortname}}} {{idnumber}}</option>
{{/competencies}}
</select>
</span>
{{/hascompetencies}}
</form>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['core/form-autocomplete', 'tool_lp/user_competency_course_navigation'], function(autocomplete, Nav) {
    (new Nav('#user-nav-{{uniqid}}', '#competency-nav-{{uniqid}}',
        '{{baseurl}}', {{userid}}, {{competencyid}}, {{courseid}}));
{{#hasusers}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#user-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}jumptouser, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hasusers}}
{{#hascompetencies}}
    autocomplete.enhance('#competency-nav-{{uniqid}}', false, false, {{# quote }}{{# str }}jumptocompetency, tool_lp{{/ str }}{{/ quote }});
{{/hascompetencies}}

});
{{/js}}
